@50 = ~Merlee~
@60 = ~Oh, hello. I am so glad to see you. Taerom showed me mercy and took me as his apprentice. He is teaching me how to make swords at the moment. I am forever in your debt, my friend. Wish I could pay you as thanks but... you understand.~
@61 = ~What do I do? What do I do?~
@62 = ~Hey. Are you okay?~
@63 = ~Can you go and despair somewhere else? I do not need to see a crybaby in the middle of the street.~
@64 = ~Sorry to bother you.~
@65 = ~No. I am not okay. I am far from okay. Everything is a mess. I tried so hard to find a decent job, pay my debts... it all went to the Hells. I failed to find enough money in time and I lost my house. I have no family, no friends, nowhere to go and my meagre belongings aren't enough for me to last on the streets.~
@66 = ~I do understand your position. I also... lost my home not so long ago... and a person I loved dearly. I am sorry to hear about your loss but you cannot give up hope. Not after everything! You lost one battle, and there will definitely be more hardship on your way but your fate isn't sealed. Think of it as a temporary drawback.~
@67 = ~Now THAT is an idea! I might do so myself one day. Roads are plagued by bandits, you can meet them practically anywhere. You're hardly a target with no money or equipment on you. Maybe they'll take you in. Imagine all the riches you'll gain.~
@68 = ~I am sorry but I do not know how to help you. I'll take my leave now.~
@69 = ~A temporary drawback. If I keep on trying... Tymora might smile at me one day. Maybe... maybe Taerom needs an apprentice. If he is willing to teach me something, potentially give me a roof over my head... Yeah. Perhaps you're right. I will hold hope tight a little longer. Thank you for your words. They are worth considering.~
@70 = ~Hope?! I lost it already and there is no going back! I will become a bandit and get what I so desperately crave! I am my own master now. Out of the way!~
@71 = ~Diamonds, pearls, gold. I would make a fortune. And... I wouldn't have to pay taxes! This is the way out! You are absolutely right! The only way to get through life is by being devious in this world and grabbing opportunities as they come along! Thank you, my friend. I shall take my leave now. Need to find some bandits to talk to!~

@72 = ~Oh, I am sorry! I did not realise the streets belong to you and you hold all the power here! Maybe I should just let myself be eaten by wolves. Not like anyone would notice!~
